  <!-- EN: CE: Mass and bulk -->
  <CE_InventoryWeightBulk.label>TODO</CE_InventoryWeightBulk.label>
  <!-- EN: You can order your colonists to pick up items and store them in their inventory. They are limited in this by their carry weight and bulk capacity.\n\nCarry weight is determined by movement capacity and the more weight a colonist is carrying, the slower they are.\n\nBulk represents the space in your colonists&apos; pockets and can be increased by equipping loadbearing gear like backpacks and tactical vests. The more stuffed their pockets are, the slower they&apos;ll work, so only pick up things you actually need.\n\nYou can check a colonist&apos;s load by selecting them, clicking the INVENTORY button and hovering over the displayed bars.\n\nTo order a colonist to pick something up, select him, right-click an item and select the &apos;Pick up&apos; option. -->
  <CE_InventoryWeightBulk.helpText>TODO</CE_InventoryWeightBulk.helpText>
